WEBVTT

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:06.300
In the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, Amen.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:13.660
The reading from the Sinaxarion for September 16, on which we commemorate the Holy

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:19.590
martyr Ludmila, Princess of the Czechs.

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:26.070
Saint Ludmila, the grandmother of St. Wenslas, Prince of the Czechs, was the wife of Prince

00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:32.510
Boryvoi. She and her husband were instructed in the Orthodox faith and baptized by the Holy

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:37.310
Bishop Methodius, the Enlightener of the Slavs.

00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:43.110
With fervent faith, the Prince and Princess did all they could to encourage their people

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:49.870
to become Christians. They built churches throughout their land and provided for the maintenance

00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:57.590
of the priests that ministered in them. Prince Boryvoi died at the age of 36, having given

00:00:57.590 --> 00:01:05.670
three sons and one daughter to Saint Ludmila, who accepted widowhood as the will of God

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:12.910
and bore her loss courageously. She detached herself from worldly pursuits and distributed

00:01:12.910 --> 00:01:21.150
her wealth to the poor. Her son, Vratislav, then ascended the throne and ruled the Czech land

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:29.430
for 23 years. On his death, he was succeeded by his son, Wenslas, whom his grandmother,

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:37.430
Saint Ludmila, had brought up in the true faith and love of the Holy Evangelic virtues.

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:44.390
But Wenslas' wife was consumed by hatred for Saint Ludmila and sent two boyars to

00:01:44.390 --> 00:01:54.190
strangle her in the castle of Tetin, now Detshin, where she had withdrawn to avoid discord.

00:01:54.190 --> 00:02:02.710
Saint Ludmila received the martyr's palm in the year 920, when she was 61 years old.

00:02:02.710 --> 00:02:08.990
How many miracles took place at her tomb that Prince Wenslas had her relics translated

00:02:08.990 --> 00:02:16.270
to Prague, where they are venerated today in the Church of St. George.

00:02:16.270 --> 00:02:23.310
Through the prayers of our Holy Father's, O Lord Jesus Christ our God, have mercy on us,

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:24.310
save us.
